Error [E1116]: A shared value has no `.read(…)` method
  --> tests/ui/shared_retired_closure_access.jet:7:18
    |
  7 |     print(config.read(value -> value.hits))
    |                  ^^^^
 Why: A shared value reads and writes like a value: a field read is one locked read, a field write is one locked write, and each statement is one atomic step
 Fix: Read the field directly (`config.name`) and write it directly (`config.hits += 1`); group several steps under `#Transact { … }`, or take an expert guard with `.guard_edit()`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E1116
